TITLE:: CommandChip
SUMMARY:: Bordered label for a committed command, parameter, or value chip.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/BorderView, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/Command, Classes/StaticText

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::CommandChip:: is a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: for every committed chip in a LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt::: the command name, a parameter name, and a typed value. Appearance such as border radius is set here so all three chips share it.

The label is white, centred LINK::Classes/StaticText:: on the given background colour. Width follows the text. Height is fixed to match the prompt's text field.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::CommandChip::.

ARGUMENT:: text
The label shown on the chip, as a LINK::Classes/String::. For a command or parameter this is its name; for a value it is the text that was committed.

ARGUMENT:: colour
The background LINK::Classes/Color::.

ARGUMENT:: height
The fixed height in pixels, as a LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::CommandChip:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: string
The label text shown on the chip.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/String::.

PRIVATE:: prInit
